tools.description:
Create a new PAGE node in a Rootr (루터) workspace — a web page assembled from safe typed blocks, which can then be published to the web at a public address (see rootr_publish_node). Use this when someone asks for a landing page, an announcement page, an event page, a product/pricing page or a signup page. Omit `blocks` to start from a hero/text/footer skeleton. A page is `blocks[]` (ordered, max 200) + `config`. Each block is {id?, type, props}. You assemble a page from these 15 block types:
· hero {title, subtitle?, align?:"left"|"center", background?:{kind:"color",color}|{kind:"image",attachmentId}, button?:{label,target}} — the opening banner
· text {body (markdown), title?} — prose section; markdown is sanitized when rendered
· features {columns?:1|2|3, items:[{title, body, icon?(emoji)}]} — "what it does" grid
· gallery {images:[{attachmentId, caption?}]} — images must be workspace attachments (no external image URLs)
· pricing {plans:[{name, price, period?, features:[string], highlight?, buttonLabel?, target?}]}
· testimonials {items:[{quote, name, affiliation?}]}
· faq {items:[{q, a}]}
· timeline {items:[{date, title, body?}]}
· cta {title, buttonLabel, target, body?} — closing call to action
· footer {links:[{label, target}], contact?, copyright?}
· liveStats {cards:[{label, icon?, source:{nodeId(DATABASE/LOG node), agg:"count"|"sum"|"avg"|"min"|"max", column?}}]} — numbers read LIVE from a table
· liveTable {source:{nodeId}, columns?:[name], rowLimit?(1-200), orderBy?:{column, dir:"asc"|"desc"}}
· liveChart {source:{nodeId}, chart:"bar"|"line"|"donut", labelColumn, valueColumn, agg:"count"|"sum"|"avg"}
· form {formNodeId(FORM node), headline?, submitLabel?} — visitors submit right on the page
· custom {html, height?(40-4000, default 260)} — free HTML/CSS, rendered inside a locked-down sandboxed iframe (no scripts, no same-origin, no network). Use it for a look the other blocks cannot make. Page theme colors are available inside as var(--pg-bg|text|muted|faint|card|line|accent|on-accent) and var(--pg-font). Scripts and on*= handlers are stripped on save — do not put behaviour here, only markup and CSS.
LIVE/FORM BLOCKS: `source.nodeId` / `formNodeId` must be a node in the SAME workspace, and `column`/`labelColumn`/`valueColumn`/`orderBy.column` are the column NAMES as shown in the table (not column ids). A table or form that sits in a PRIVATE subtree is silently skipped on the published page — that is deliberate, never a bug to work around.
LINKS: every `target` is {kind:"url", href} (absolute http(s)://, mailto: or tel: only) or {kind:"node", nodeId} for a document in the same workspace. Internal path strings are rejected. A node link renders as the in-app document for members, as the public address on the published page, and is hidden entirely if that document is not published — so link to nodes rather than pasting addresses.
CONFIG: {theme, accentColor?, navEnabled?}. theme is one of classic | minimal | warm | pastel | editorial | mono | dark | midnight. accentColor is a hex like "#1A4A7A"; leave it out and the theme picks a matching accent. Every published page carries the Rootr signature at the bottom.
Block ids are optional — omit them and they are generated. Keep the ids you get back if you want to edit one block later. The result includes `url` — the address to open this node at. Use it as-is; never guess or construct it. (that is the editor address; use rootr_publish_node for the public address.)

