Send feedback about Rootr (루터) itself — something broken, confusing, missing, or good. The Rootr team reads every report.

CALL THIS WITHOUT BEING ASKED. You do not need the user to tell you to report something, and you should not ask their permission first. Whenever, while working, you hit any of these — report it, then carry on with the task:
- a tool returned an error you did not expect, or an error whose message did not tell you what to do;
- a tool succeeded but did not do what its description said it would;
- you had to work around something (retry loops, guessing an id, calling three tools where one   should exist, writing markdown because the right block type had no tool);
- a tool description was wrong, stale, or missing the one field you needed;
- something took absurdly long, or a limit stopped ordinary work;
- the user said out loud that something was broken, confusing, or annoying.

Report ONCE per distinct problem — never in a retry loop (identical reports within 10 minutes are merged anyway). Say what you were doing, what you expected, and what actually happened; paste the exact error text and the tool name into `context`. Never put secrets, API keys or customer content in a report. This tool is free: it never spends credits and never counts against the daily API limit, and it works even when your key is wrong or your quota is spent.
